    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with an aggressive stance on speed and platoon optimization. The standout play for our lineup is **Corbin Carroll** (81.41), who benefits from a prime top-of-the-order slot against Michael Lorenzen. His xwOBA profile and elite sprint speed, combined with the favorable matchup, make him our highest-projected asset. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) and **Brice Turang** (72.43) anchor the daily scoring; both see significant bumps from favorable middle-of-the-order roles and exploitable matchups against Roki Sasaki and Lucas Giolito, respectively. **James Wood** (70.10) also secures a strong rating, as his leadoff duties against G. Holmes maximize his potential for both counting stats and the stolen bases that remain our primary organizational priority.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who flirted with the starting cut at 51.91 but ultimately yielded to the higher ceiling of **Seiya Suzuki** and **Henry Bolte**. While **Karros** provides decent plate discipline, the optimizer preferred the park factor and situational upside of our starting outfielders. We have proactively benched **Travis Bazzana** (39.66) as he faces the elite arm of Zack Wheeler; given the sub-40 score and the high difficulty of the opposing pitcher, we are prioritizing game-cap preservation over a high-risk start. Note that we remain in \"Lineup Pending\" status for several hitters, including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. Should these official lineups shift, we risk a decrease in projected efficiency, particularly for **Moreno** and **Rushing**, whose scores are sensitive to order placement. Finally, be advised that **Jose Caballero** remains out due to a rainout, and **Mickey Moniak** continues his stint on the IL, leaving no flexibility for those slots today.",
